  ("How much does heat pump installation cost in Oshawa?", "Cold-climate heat pump installation in Oshawa starts at $5,500 installed. Installed pricing depends on size and installation requirements, such as duct repairs, an added return or panel work in an older home, and every item is listed on a guaranteed written quote."),
  ("Will a heat pump work with the old ductwork in my Oshawa house?", "Usually, once the ducts are measured. We test static pressure and compare duct sizes to the airflow the heat pump needs, then size the unit to match or add a return where a room is starved. If the ducts truly cannot carry it, a ductless system is the honest alternative."),
  ("Should I keep my gas furnace when I add a heat pump?", "Yes, if the furnace is in good condition. A hybrid system uses the heat pump for cooling and most heating days and the furnace for the coldest nights, and we set the switch-over point from your Oshawa Power and Enbridge rates."),
  ("How long does a heat pump installation take in an older Oshawa home?", "A hybrid installation on existing ducts is usually a one-day job. Adding a return, replacing the furnace at the same time or upgrading the panel can stretch it, and the quote states the schedule so you are not guessing."),
  ("Does an Oshawa home on Enbridge gas qualify for the heat pump rebate?", "It can. Gas-heated homes get the smaller Home Renovation Savings Program tier, commonly up to $2,000, while homes heated by electricity, oil, propane or wood can receive up to $7,500. The model must be on NRCan's qualified list and pre-approval must be in place before installation, and program terms can change."),
